## Context and authority

Filed from replicator 0002 after the author requested consolidation before numerical confirmation. Related to tracker 1552 and closed scope ticket 1561. This is a request for receiving-project Imagine, not an implementation authorization or an assertion that the existing whole-paper categories are false.

## Observation

At IDH main e6521eeca366035930ce4a0e281bda0ec53220ab, references/assessment.md lines 84-114 require whole-paper provision, while lines 122-124 already permit main-result CRA/CRR. Lines 194-220 give the derived table whole-paper coverage. A host-author override was needed to assess provision for a declared selected claim. Scoped Fully must not silently satisfy an existing whole-paper criterion.

Replicator's reviewed Arechar audit (e4cb874de0a034fbe7a97fa5b35569c4dd3fad1f) selects numerical Figures 5a/5d before dependency inspection. Their actual producer/consumer chain excludes national WVS distributions needed by supplementary Figure S4. Reassessment (a167acb57a39cb70590ef8ba066fbe990f308e8f) finds analysis input information and numerical code complete for that target, upstream raw/cleaning unknown. The broader 3/4 pilot remains unchanged. No scientific program was run and no new accuracy claim is made.

The existing primary route is ACRe Assessment, https://bitss.github.io/ACRE/assessment.html : introduction permits selected claims, display items or estimates; section 3.2 maps each item to inputs; 3.3.1 grades individual items; 3.3.3 treats paper-level practices separately. Brodeur pre-Games slides 4/9 emphasize main results/models without defining every provision category.

## Request for receiver Imagine

Represent a declared claim/output/estimate scope explicitly and propagate it through provision, execution and reference comparison. Retain a labeled whole-paper audit. Consider main-claim default for Games as a proposal; do not silently change the canonical CIRED grid, existing scope decisions, tolerances, adaptation conventions or old observations. Resolve how selected-target results coexist with existing whole-paper criteria before implementation.

Receiver owns fact/framing checks, duplicate and work-in-flight checks, ownership, standing rulings and disposition. Source preflight found only tracker 1552 open; closed 1561 deliberately established current whole-paper scope. Preserve the already merged 1565/1566 evidence fixes; these are not being refiled.

## Proposed acceptance questions

- [ ] Declared target is inspectable and consistently named at every stage; whole-paper mode remains available.
- [ ] A gap outside the target cannot become a selected-result gap; unknown required coverage stays unknown.
- [ ] Cross-scope categories cannot produce an unqualified agreement score; printed reference categories and narrative inferences stay distinguishable.
- [ ] Numerical estimates and literal rendering, information provision and software readiness, remain distinct.
- [ ] Existing grid meanings and old evidence are preserved or explicitly migrated under an approved decision.

## Evidence and handoff boundary

Assigned source project: /home/haduong/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator. Read reviewed reports with git show on the hashes above: replications/arechar-mainclaim-audit-2026-11-26/REPORT.md and replications/arechar-reevaluation-2026-11-26/REPORT.md. The consolidation branch t0002-consolidation carries doc/examples/arechar-mainclaim/README.md and IDH-SCOPE-BRIEF.md; its final commit will be logged after consolidation. These are references, not files to change from IDH.

No IDH skill, scientific source, comparator or canonical grid is changed by this ticket. Replicator owns downstream input/comparator follow-up. Main-claim CRA can proceed from adequate analytic inputs without resolving the upstream raw boundary first; CRR and raw-completeness claims cannot.
